export default {"T000733":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"comparison\" data-relation-style=\"equivalence\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Equivalence</span><h3>Universal spectral submersion criterion for arc-covers</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent algebra-related\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Objects of comparison</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#G000025\"><span>Arc topology</span><code>G000025</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000056\"><span>Spectral space</span><code>P000056</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⋯</span><a href=\"../database/#T000733\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000733</a></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Valuative topology refinement</p><p><strong>Hypotheses.</strong> Let <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f:Y\\to X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> be a morphism of qcqs schemes.</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> The map <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is an arc-cover if and only if for every map <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">′</mo></msup><mo>→</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X&#x27;\\to X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> from a qcqs scheme the base-changed map <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f&#x27;</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is surjective and any subset <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U\\subseteq X&#x27;</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> whose inverse image is quasi-compact Zariski open is Zariski open. The resulting open <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is quasi-compact because it is the continuous image of its quasi-compact inverse image.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1807.04725\">Bhatt–Mathew, The arc-topology, Definition 2.14 and Proposition 2.19</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000733\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T000733\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>"};
